er appearing to conquer the Sun burns  felt even more invincible and entitled  to do whatever he pleased in his case  that meant stealing a lollipop from  Maggie Simpson unfortunately for him he  was unaware that his pistol was  precariously placed in its holster and  in the old man's struggle with the baby  the gun went off into his chest giving  him some much-needed comeuppance in the  episode the trouble with trillions it's  revealed that after World War Two  President Harry Truman minted a one  trillion dollar bill in an effort to  reconstruct post-war Europe  the US government then tasked a spry  young mr. burns with flying the money to  Europe surprise surprise it never  arrived  obviously stealing an incomprehensible  amount of money meant to help people  after one of the most devastating pieces  of human history alone has got to be one  of mr. burns worst acts but wait there's  more after Homer helps discover that  burn still has the bill  the FBI burst in to arrest him but burns  manages to escape by fleeing the country  the second part of his escape plan  buying a tiny little Caribbean island he  found on a map unfortunately that Island  happens to be Cuba which some will note  is kinda spoken for when it comes to  land agreements armed with a trillion  dollars in cash though burns attempts to  just purchase the country from its  president Fidel Castro Castro proves to  be a little too cunning for burns though  he just asked to see the bill and then  pretends it was never handed to him with  that burns returns to the States  defeated but like most super-rich  criminals he never actually faces any  consequences two dozen and one  greyhounds from the sixth season of The  Simpsons is responsible for one of the  better toe tappers in the show's long  musical history it's also one of Burns's  most evil acts to date especially if  you're an animal lover you gotta admit  it's catchy when the Simpson family dog  Santa's Little Helper gets a little  frisky with ano